.TH PRJ 1 "October 2026" "prj 3.0.4"
.SH NAME
prj \- create and manage dated project directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B prj
.RB [ -h | -v ]
.br
.B prj
.BR help " [" command "]"
.br
.B prj
.BR new " [" -hnv "] [" -t " " template "] [" --var " " key=value "] " project
.br
.B prj
.IR command " [" -h "]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B prj
creates dated project directories from Mustache templates and lists configured
project roots. With no arguments it shows help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR new , " mk" , " make" , " n"
Create a dated project directory. See \fBNEW\fR.
.TP
.BR list , " ls" , " l"
Print absolute paths for immediate child directories in each configured project
root. It accepts no arguments other than \fB-h\fR. Roots are processed in
configured order; entries within a root are sorted.
.TP
.BR templates , " t"
Print available named template names, one per line, using template lookup
precedence. It accepts no arguments other than \fB-h\fR.
.TP
.BR doctor , " d"
Report project-root, template-source, deprecated-setting, and renderer status.
It accepts no arguments other than \fB-h\fR.
.TP
.BR info , " i"
Print the current effective project-root and template configuration. It accepts
no arguments other than \fB-h\fR.
.TP
.BR version , " v" , " -v"
Show the command version. It accepts no arguments other than \fB-h\fR.
.TP
.BR help , " h" , " -h"
Show general help or help for one command. \fBprj help \fIcommand\fR is
equivalent to \fBprj \fIcommand\fB -h\fR. The command argument may be a
canonical command name or an alias.
.SH NEW
.B prj new
accepts the following arguments:
.TP
.I project
Required project name. A name prefixed with \fBYYYY-MM-DD\fR or
\fBYYYYMMDD\fR uses that date; otherwise today is used. A path selects the
destination project root.
.TP
.BR -n , " --dry-run"
Print the directory that would be created without creating it.
.TP
.BI -t " template"
Use a named template or a template directory path.
.TP
.BI --var " key=value"
Add a template variable. This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show help for \fBnew\fR.
.TP
.BR -v , " --version"
Show the command version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PRJ_PROJECTS_DIR
Default project root for creation.
.TP
.B PRJ_PROJECTS_DIRS
Colon-separated project roots. The first root is used for creation when
\fBPRJ_PROJECTS_DIR\fR is unset.
.TP
.B PRJ_TEMPLATE_DIR
Parent directory for bundled or installed named templates.
.TP
.B PRJ_TEMPLATES_DIR
Parent directory for user named templates. It defaults to
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/prj/templates\fR or \fB~/.config/prj/templates\fR.
.SH DEPRECATION
.B mkprj
is a compatibility command for \fBprj new\fR. The old \fBPROJECTS_DIR\fR,
\fBPROJECTS_DIRS\fR, \fBMKPRJ_TEMPLATE_DIR\fR, \fBTEMPLATES_DIR\fR, and
\fBmkprj\fR template paths remain supported with warnings.
